From: Kythira <noreply@bit63.org>
Subject: [PATCH] fix: preserve the query string in url-sourced external account credentials

UrlExternalAccountCredentials folds the credential source URL's query string
into what it then hands URI::Create as the *path*, with query parameters
explicitly empty:

    url_full_path_ = absl::StrCat("/", v[3]);   // still contains "?a=b&c=d"
    ...
    URI::Create(url_.scheme(), url_.authority(), url_full_path_,
                {} /* query params */, "" /* fragment */);

The wire request takes its target from that URI -- httpcli.cc uses
uri.EncodedPathAndQueryParams(), not request.path -- so the '?', '&' and '%'
inside the "path" are percent-encoded and the server receives one mangled path
segment carrying no query parameters at all.

Against GitHub Actions' OIDC token endpoint that means `audience` and
`api-version` never arrive, and the request is refused with

    403 {"source":"actions-run-service",
         "errorMessage":"runner does not have permissions to generate id token"}

which reads as a credential fault and is not one. The Authorization header is
sent and is valid, which is exactly why the answer is 403 and not 401; replaying
the same URL and headers with curl returns 200. Callers reaching the same
endpoint through libcurl (google-cloud-cpp's REST path) are unaffected, so only
the gRPC-backed clients fail -- which is what made this look like a
service-specific permissions problem for months.

url_ is already URI::Parse of the same string, so its path and query parameters
are available and correctly split. Use those, and let URI encode each query
value once instead of encoding the delimiters of an already-assembled query.

request.path deliberately keeps url_full_path_: that is the raw path-and-query,
and it is what the HTTP layer wants on the occasions it does consult it.

Still present in v1.78.1. Reported upstream.

--- a/src/core/lib/security/credentials/external/url_external_account_credentials.cc
+++ b/src/core/lib/security/credentials/external/url_external_account_credentials.cc
@@ -144,9 +144,13 @@
 UrlExternalAccountCredentials::RetrieveSubjectToken(
     Timestamp deadline,
     absl::AnyInvocable<void(absl::StatusOr<std::string>)> on_done) {
+  // Take the path and the query from the parsed URL rather than passing a path
+  // that still has the query string inside it: the request target is built with
+  // URI::EncodedPathAndQueryParams(), so a query smuggled through the path
+  // argument has its delimiters percent-encoded and never arrives.
   auto url_for_request =
-      URI::Create(url_.scheme(), url_.authority(), url_full_path_,
-                  {} /* query params */, "" /* fragment */);
+      URI::Create(url_.scheme(), url_.authority(), url_.path(),
+                  url_.query_parameter_pairs(), "" /* fragment */);
   if (!url_for_request.ok()) {
     return MakeOrphanable<NoOpFetchBody>(
         event_engine(), std::move(on_done),
